---
title: Best Kotlin Books (2026) — Hand-Picked Recommendations
description: A curated, hand-picked list of the best Kotlin books for beginners, Android developers, and backend engineers — updated for 2026.
layout: base.njk
---

<div class="intro">
	<h1>Best Kotlin Books</h1>
	<p class="intro-lede">A curated, hand-picked list of the best Kotlin books for beginners, Android developers, and backend engineers — ranked by how genuinely useful each one is, not by publish date.</p>
</div>

<div class="book-grid">
	{% for book in books %}
	<article class="book-card">
		<a class="book-card-link" href="{{ ('/books/' + book.slug + '/') | url }}">
			<img class="book-card-cover" src="{{ book.coverImage | url }}" alt="{{ book.title }} book cover" width="300" height="450" loading="lazy">
			<div class="book-card-body">
				<span class="book-card-rank">#{{ loop.index }} pick</span>
				<h2>{{ book.title }}</h2>
				<p class="book-meta">{{ book.authors | join(", ") }} &middot; {{ book.year }}</p>
				<span class="badge badge-{{ book.level }}">{{ book.level }}</span>
				<p class="best-for"><strong>Best for:</strong> {{ book.bestFor }}</p>
				<p class="book-card-summary">{{ book.summary }}</p>
			</div>
		</a>
	</article>
	{% endfor %}
</div>
